# mobsfscan project exemptions (round-68 T13; round-70 T-mobsf migration) —
#   see round68-audit.md §T13, round69-audit.md §T-b and round70-audit.md §T-mobsf.
#
# android_logging (CWE-532): mobsfscan 1.2.0 flags every Log.* call that
# interpolates a variable (259 findings on this tree, measured 2026-11-22).
# Project-wide documented stance (round-56 SEC-06, proguard-rules.pro:135-139):
# release builds strip Log.v/d/i/w via -assumenosideeffects; only Log.e survives.
#
# round-69 (CodeRabbit PR#57 #3): the one finding that carried user game data —
#   StockfishNative.sendUciCommand's Log.e("Error sending command: " + command),
#   whose command can embed a FEN (the full game position) — was FIXED AT THE
#   ROOT: static message + command.length() only. (Debug builds keep a
#   documented Log.d of the full command — release-stripped, diagnostic-only.)
# round-70 (CodeRabbit PR#59 #1): the second game-content-capable path —
#   postJsCallbackDirect's Log.e("Error posting JS callback: " + cleanJs),
#   whose onEngineEval payload embeds the FEN as 8th argument — root-fixed the
#   same way (event name + payload length only, see callbackEventName). The
#   remaining release Log.e output is engine paths, thread/setting names,
#   exit codes and static labels (site-by-site review, round70-audit §T-logE).
#
# round-70 (CodeRabbit PR#59 #2) — GLOBAL ignore-rules DELETED, per-line
#   suppression IN. mobsfscan 1.2.0 supports an inline
#       // mobsf-ignore: android_logging
#   comment on any line of the flagged span (verified empirically in-sandbox:
#   annotated lines suppressed, unannotated flagged). All 259 findings were
#   reviewed and now carry the marker at the flagged line, so any FUTURE
#   unsafe Log line will ALERT in the MobSF SARIF instead of being silently
#   swallowed by a global rule here. Review boundary (round-71): editing an
#   already marked statement may remain suppressed; every such edit therefore
#   requires renewed line-level review. Accepted engine diagnostics may contain
#   PV moves, but no FEN or user identity data. Current/stripped mobsfscan 1.2.0
#   double-scan: android_logging 0/259; both runs must report successful execution.
#   This file
#   intentionally carries NO active directives; it survives as the audit
#   trail for the stance. If code scanning shows android_logging findings:
#   they are NEW, read them, do not blanket-ignore them here.
#
# NOTE: dotfiles have failed to land through the zip overlay channel before
# (the .gitignore incident, round-67 T0). If the post-upload remote re-check
# shows this file missing, create it via the GitHub web editor with this
# exact content (see the round-68 delivery README).
